-- title:
--   Automorphisms fixing the level-M/p subfield are the identity
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ be a subgroup containing the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, i.e. every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ with $u \mapsto 1$ lies in $H$ (so $H$ is the full preimage of its image). Write $F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series obtained by base change of the rational $X_H(M)$ function field `xHFunctionField M H` along the coefficient embedding, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated by the images of its elements; and let $F'$ be the corresponding field at level $M/p$ for `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$. Let $\tau$ be an automorphism of $F$ as an algebra over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and assume that for all $f \in F$ and $u \in F'$ whose underlying Laurent series agree, the Laurent series of $\tau f$ again equals that of $u$; that is, $\tau$ fixes pointwise every element of $F$ whose $q$-expansion lies in $F'$. The conclusion is that $\tau$ is the identity automorphism of $F$.
--
--   This is the triviality of the deck transformation group of the degree-$p+1$ covering $X_H(M) \to X_{H'}(M/p)$ in its geometric ($\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-coefficient) form, phrased on function fields of $q$-expansions. It is used to pin down uniquely the Atkin–Lehner-type identifications of the two models at level $M$ over level $M/p$, and is cited by the corresponding $\Gamma_H$-level statements and by the existence results for the rational algebra equivalences on charts.
